{"resourceIdentifier":"2697","resourceName":"Zhengbang AWMS GHG Mitigation Project in Sichuan Province","description":"The project introduces new animal waste management systems to treat the manure from 4 swine farms in Sichuan Province. Each subsidiary swine farm will install one animal waste management system, and the manure is treated on site. The purpose of the project activity is to treat the manure and wastewater to avoid methane emissions generated in the baseline uncovered anaerobic lagoons. \r\nThe project activity uses flushing system to collect the manure automatically. All the manure and wastewater are collected and then put into the homogenate regulating tank. After further hydrolysis and grit settling, all were put into the anaerobic digestion. The biogas generated during the anaerobic process will be captured for power generation. After anaerobic fermentation, the fermentation liquid is separated by solid and liquid, and the biogas residue is put into the aerobic composting system used to produce solid organic fertilizer. The biogas slurry is used for agricultural irrigation.\r\nIt is estimated that approximately 522 tons of animal manure will be handled daily by the AWMS. The biogas generated during the anaerobic process will be collected for electricity production. The annual electricity production is estimated to be 14,645MWh. Also, the generated electricity will be only used for daily operation of AWMS and 4 swine farms themselves and will not be connected to the region grid net or other users. For conservativeness, baseline emissions from power generation are neglected. The project activity will reduce of GHG in the atmosphere through avoiding methane emissions from anaerobic treatment of swine manure and wastewater.","location":{"latitude":28.709471,"longitude":107.280805},"inPublicCommentPeriod":false,"lastPublicCommentPeriod":{"startInclusive":"2021-12-09","endExclusive":"2022-01-09","endInclusive":"2022-01-08"},"attributes":[{"code":"PROJECT_